      en: "Gutulia National Park, established in 1968, is Norway's smallest national park, covering only 23 km². Located in Hedmark near the Swedish border, it preserves a primeval pine forest, one of the last of its kind in Northern Europe. The terrain features glacial landforms, bogs, and small lakes. The park is noted for its rich lichen and moss flora. It serves as a key habitat for capercaillie and lynx. The summit of Gutulia provides panoramic views of the untouched wilderness. The park maintains a minimalist approach: marked trails exist, but there are no lodges or extensive facilities.",
