      en: "The Rogaland coastline in southwestern Norway stretches about 100 km from the Boknafjord region to Jæren. It features diverse geology: sandy beaches, rocky cliffs, and skerries. The Jæren beach is one of the longest sandy beaches in Norway. The coast is a crucial stopover for migratory birds, especially in spring and autumn. Agriculture in Jæren thrives due to the mild climate influenced by the Gulf Stream. Historically, the area was a center for fishing and shipping. The Kvassheim lighthouse is a notable landmark. Several nature reserves protect the dune landscapes.",
